+# Flow features: Workload, Deadline risk, Daily goal
+
+Plain text for the Help sheet and README (merge by hand). What Sunsama, Motion and Todoist have and the Planner lacked.
+
+## Workload (`#workload`)
+- **Workload** (Today; tile in All tools; palette "Workload today"; link `#workload`): today's tasks against the free time
+  left today, as a bar and one line: "5h of tasks, 4h 40m free: over by 20m". Free time is 7am to 10pm from now, after
+  shifts, events, travel and time blocks. A task without an estimate counts as 30 minutes; ideas are left out; a task
+  already time-blocked today counts as its block, never twice.
+- On an over-planned day it is a full card in red with **Trim**. Any other day it is one line under Dashboards
+  ("4h planned, 4h 40m free").
+- **Trim to fit** shows what fits (highest priority first, then oldest) and what moves to tomorrow. Nothing changes until
+  **Apply**; the toast offers **Undo**.
+
+## Deadline risk (`#deadlines`)
+- Tasks dated in the next 14 days, earliest date first, against 60% of each day's free time (the same share as Catch up).
+  A task is at risk when it, plus everything due before it, needs more time than there is before its date. Today's own
+  tasks use up time but are Workload's to report. A task with a time block before its date is planned, never at risk.
+- At risk: a line in Needs you now ("Write the eval report may miss Thu Nov 5", **Fix**). The sheet lists each one with
+  what it needs and how short it is.
+- **Block** puts the task in the first free gap before its date that holds all of it, else the longest one ("Block today
+  10am, 3h"). It is a normal time block linked to the task (Undo works). **Open** opens the task to move its date or cut
+  its estimate.
+
+## Daily goal (`#daily-goal`)
+- One line under Dashboards ("2 of 3 done · 2 days in a row"); open it for a ring, the last 7 days as bars (green = goal
+  met) and the run of days in a row. Counted from the tasks you tick off (their done time).
+- **Goal** sets 1 to 10 tasks a day (this phone). The run counts back from today once today's goal is met, else from
+  yesterday, so it is never lost before the day is over.
+
+## Notes for the lead (not for the Help sheet)
+- Code: `planner/ext-flow.js`, loaded by one `<script src="ext-flow.js">` in `<head>` after ext-power.js. It waits for
+  `planner:ready` (`window.PlannerAPI`). Nothing else in `index.html` changed.
+- Data: no new synced collection and no new field. Task moves and time blocks go through `snapshot()` + `commit()`. The
+  only new key is the device-only `planner.flow.goal` (1-10, default 3).
+- Today cards: `flrisk` (Needs you now, soft label "Deadline risk", only while something is at risk), `flwork` (Today
+  while over-planned, else Dashboards), `flgoal` (Dashboards). All are in Customize Today. Tiles `flwork`, `flrisk`
+  (Calendar) and `flgoal` (Me); commands `fx-work`, `fx-risk`, `fx-goal`.
+- Pure helpers on `window.__fl`: `trim(tasks, freeMinutes)`, `risk(tasks, days)`, `goal(doneByDay, today, goal)`, `est(task)`.
+- Tests: `planner/tests/flow.test.js` (PORT env, default 8790; 41 checks).
